  "generated_text": "To find the integer \\( n \\) such that \\( -90 \\le n \\le 90 \\) and \\(\\sin n^\\circ = \\sin 419^\\circ\\), we need to use the periodic and symmetric properties of the sine function. The sine function is periodic with a period of \\(360^\\circ\\), meaning \\(\\sin x = \\sin (x + 360k)\\) for any integer \\(k\\). Additionally, the sine function is symmetric about \\(180^\\circ\\), meaning \\(\\sin x = \\sin (180^\\circ - x)\\).\n\nFirst, we reduce \\(419^\\circ\\) to an angle between \\(0^\\circ\\) and \\(360^\\circ\\):\n\\[419^\\circ = 419^\\circ - 360^\\circ = 59^\\circ.\\]\nSo, \\(\\sin 419^\\circ = \\sin 59^\\circ\\).\n\nNext, we use the identity \\(\\sin x = \\sin (180^\\circ - x)\\) to find an equivalent angle for \\(59^\\circ\\) within the range \\([-90^\\circ, 90^\\circ]\\):\n\\[59^\\circ = 180^\\circ - 121^\\circ,\\]\nbut since \\(121^\\circ\\) is outside the range \\([-90^\\circ, 90^\\circ]\\), we use the fact that \\(\\sin x = \\sin (-x)\\) to find an equivalent negative angle:\n\\[59^\\circ = 180^\\circ - 121^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 180^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = 239^\\circ - 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ + 360^\\circ = -121^\\circ +